---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Company | BeaconGuard Assurance"
  description="BeaconGuard builds the independent authorization and verification layer for complete governed AI transactions across healthcare, financial services, and regulated internal automation."
>
  <section class="stack-section">
    <h1>The authorization layer between AI output and enterprise action</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      BeaconGuard is the independent authorization and verification layer for
      regulated AI actions. It governs whether an enterprise application may
      invoke AI and whether a declared enterprise action based on an
      AI-generated result may proceed. Control before execution. Evidence after
      every decision.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="stack-section">
    <h2>Mission</h2>
    <p>
      BeaconGuard exists to make complete AI transaction authorization
      dependable, reviewable, and operationally practical for high-risk
      enterprise workflows—without treating probabilistic model behavior as the
      authorization authority.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="stack-section">
    <h2>Priority regulated workflows</h2>
    <p>
      BeaconGuard is evaluating bounded workflows across healthcare, financial
      services, and regulated internal automation. Industry pages describe
      illustrative scenarios, not customer production validation and not a
      commercially locked first market.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="stack-section">
    <h2>Why BeaconGuard exists</h2>
    <p>
      Enterprises want to adopt AI in sensitive workflows, but model behavior is
      probabilistic. Control ownership, auditability, and enforcement cannot be
      left to prompt design alone. An AI-generated result remains an untrusted
      proposal until BeaconGuard authorizes its intended use. Provider success
      is not enterprise authorization. BeaconGuard authorizes; the enterprise
      application executes; the enterprise system of record remains
      authoritative.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="stack-section">
    <h2>What we do not claim</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        This site does not represent healthcare employers, healthcare systems,
        accelerators, or contacts as customers, design partners, sponsors, or
        endorsers.
      </li>
      <li>
        BeaconGuard is currently offered through controlled evaluation.
        Production deployment requires customer-specific qualification.
      </li>
      <li>
        BeaconGuard does not certify clinical correctness, legal admissibility,
        or third-party compliance attestations unless separately evidenced.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="stack-section">
    <h2>Learn more</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><a href="/platform">Platform</a></li>
      <li><a href="/healthcare">Healthcare AI control</a></li>
      <li><a href="/fintech">Financial workflow control</a></li>
      <li><a href="/verification">Verification</a></li>
      <li><a href="/trust-assurance">Trust Center</a></li>
      <li><a href="/design-partner-program">Controlled Evaluation</a></li>
    </ul>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
